WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.379
Immigration intake has doubled in recent years.

00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:07.750
Over eight hundred thousand Temporary Foreign Workers are currently in Canada.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:12.250
Wage suppression through the TFW Program expansion is documented.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:17.511
The IRCC processing backlog exceeds six months for standard applications.

00:00:17.511 --> 00:00:21.454
Integration services are inadequate at current intake levels.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:26.090
Refugee claim processing delays have been cited in parliamentary testimony.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:32.011
The healthcare and education burden on provinces is documented in provincial briefs to the federal government.

00:00:32.011 --> 00:00:35.590
The question is not whether Canada should accept immigrants.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:40.852
The question is whether the infrastructure exists to serve them — and the data says it does not.
